#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:178
#: 501b0bd843c842e192f67f111e587de2
msgid "Operation using Annotation"
msgstr "使用标注的操作"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:180
#: e96f349a59fb4fb4942f4c626eb4c3e7
msgid ""
"DingoDB presents a Java API which is comprehensive and powerful, but requires a "
"measure of boiler plate code to map the data from Java POJOs to the database. "
"The Annotation is aim to lower the amount of code required when mapping POJOs "
"to DingoDB and back as well as reducing some of the brittleness of the code."
msgstr ""
"DingoDB提供的Java应用程序接口（API）全面而强大，但需要大量的模板代码才能将数据从"
"Java POJOs映射到数据库。注释的目的是减少将 POJOs 映射到 DingoDB 时所需的代码量，"
"同时减少代码的脆弱性。"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:182
#: bdd9f7b01ee748c381eda499aee74376
msgid "Keys"
msgstr "键"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:184
#: 6d5fac82ad794e8dba66a60cec31daf5
msgid ""
"The key to an DingoDB record can be specified either as a field or a property. "
"Remember that DingoDB keys can be Strings, numberical types and date types only."
msgstr ""
"DingoDB 记录的键可以指定为字段或属性。请注意：DingoDB 的键只能是字符串、数字类型"
"和日期类型。"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:186
#: 7c3545db76c149e49d3fef2f0c613edd
msgid ""
"To use a field as the key, simply mark the field with the DingoKey annotation:"
msgstr "要使用某个字段作为键，只需用 DingoKey 注释标记该字段即可。"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:195
#: e43e3324cf464116b11124f01127aea4
msgid "Column"
msgstr "列"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:197
#: f126265c985249df96170d9ae5473b1a
msgid ""
"Fields in Java can be mapped to the database irrespective of the visibility of "
"the column. To do so, simply specify the column to map to with the @DingoColumn "
"annotation:"
msgstr ""
"无论列的可见性如何，Java 中的字段都可以映射到数据库。只需使用 @DingoColumn 注解"
"指定要映射的列即可："

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:204
#: 182ce61fa631410fae65782dadcd3539
msgid ""
"This will map the contents of the `version` field to a `vrsn` column in DingoDB."
msgstr "这将把 `version` 字段的内容映射到 DingoDB 中的 `vrsn` 列。"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:206
#: 71a06d14dcb9461da6d68d8ca9e790a7
msgid ""
"If the name of the column matches the name of the field in Java, the name can "
"be omitted:"
msgstr "如果列名与 Java 中的字段名一致，则可以省略列名："

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:213
#: a1db14b6e2644d8fae8edbce54c6e0d6
msgid "This will appear in DingoDB as the `age` column."
msgstr "这将在 DingoDB 中显示为 `age` 列。"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:215
#: f3c56e549ad64897b63baa856585877a
msgid ""
"By default, all fields will be mapped to the database. Fields can be excluded "
"with the @DingoExclude annotation, and renamed with the @DingoColumn "
"annotation. For example:"
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，所有字段都将映射到数据库。可以使用 @DingoExclude 注解排除字段，并使"
"用 @DingoColumn 注解重命名字段。例如："

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:226
#: 1e96a2b9f2874997b04e742c5da22b14
msgid ""
"This saves the record with 4 columns, `a`,`b`,`c`,`d`. To save only fields "
"`a`,`b`,`c` you can do either:"
msgstr ""
"这样保存的记录有 4 列：`a`,`b`,`c`,`d`。要只保存`a`,`b`,`c`字段，可以选择以下两"
"种方法："

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:239
#: ff0cac2b24194b68b02b76c9f506afcb
msgid ""
"If a field is marked with both @DingoExclude, the column will not be mapped to "
"the database."
msgstr ""
"如果一个字段同时标记了 @DingoExclude 和 @DingoExclude，该列将不会被映射到数据"
"库。"

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:241
#: 5eea99745fa348209feb9fc5a6a41533
msgid ""
"You can force the name of a particular column or columns by specifying them in "
"an DingoColumn:"
msgstr "您可以在 DingoColumn 中指定一列或多列的名称："

#: ../../source/get_started/play_with_dingo_using_dingoclient.md:254
#: 63da3f6912754efe8988fbc853b1c1bd
msgid "This will save 4 fields in the database, `a`, `b`, `longCname`, `d`."
msgstr "这将在数据库中保存 4 个字段，即 `a`、`b`、`longCname` 和 `d`。"

